{"id":"pacific-coast-bike","title":"Pacific Coast by bike: Seattle to San Diego","who":"Classic route · America's favourite bike tour","when":"Late spring to early autumn (ride southbound with the wind)","vehicle":"Touring bike, 4–8 weeks, hiker-biker campsites","kind":"bike","color":"#0369a1","summary":"About 3,000 km down the coast of Washington, Oregon and California: Olympic forests, Oregon's sea stacks and cheap hiker-biker campsites, redwoods, the Golden Gate, Big Sur's cliffs and the beach towns of the south. Almost all paved; watch the narrow tunnels and bridges. Highway 1 through Big Sur reopened in full in January 2026 after nearly three years of slide repairs; short closures after storms still happen.","sources":[{"label":"Caltrans: Highway 1 reopens at Regent's Slide (January 2026)","url":"https://dot.ca.gov/caltrans-near-me/district-5/d5-news/d5-news-1-14-26"},{"label":"Edinburgh Bicycle: bike the Pacific Coast Highway, part 4","url":"https://www.edinburghbicycle.com/info/blog/bike-pacific-coast-highway-us-part-4-4"},{"label":"Adventure Cycling: Pacific Coast Bicycle Route","url":"https://www.adventurecycling.org/routes-and-maps/adventure-cycling-route-network/pacific-coast/"}],"approximate":"Main towns; the line follows cycle routes near the coast.","km":2512,"bbox":[-124.4979,32.7157,-117.1638,47.6038],"stops":[{"name":"Seattle","place":"Seattle, Washington","at":[47.6038,-122.3301],"text":"Ferry across Puget Sound to the Olympic peninsula.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg/500px-Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg","page":"Seattle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Astoria","place":"Astoria, Oregon","at":[46.1882,-123.832],"text":"Over the Columbia river into Oregon.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Astoria_Oregon.jpg/500px